# Append-only data files: concurrent appends must not conflict.
#
# `axiom-rewrite/candidates.jsonl` is the candidate ledger — the same kind of
# artifact as `docs/decisions/LOG.md` (append-only history) and is committed for
# the same reason: a reader must be able to verify "we tried this" without
# trusting a local file. Under the repo's parallel-agent model two agents can
# append between the same two commits, and a normal 3-way merge would conflict on
# the final line. `merge=union` (a git builtin) keeps both sides' added lines, so
# parallel appends compose instead of colliding. Order within the file is then
# whatever each side wrote; the ledger is read by `candidate_id`, not position.
axiom-rewrite/candidates.jsonl merge=union
# Gate-6 signals (#34) are the same kind of append-only artifact: a signal is
# written after its candidate record already exists, so the two files can be
# appended by parallel agents between the same two commits.
axiom-rewrite/gate6_signals.jsonl merge=union
